{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/test-bin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:04:07.305067Z","id":"6e05f24a5f6ccf69b2a41d92e1c3c94b8aab3d4527e7b8eaa18ecfc4349effbf","body":{"detail":"When `cargo build` fails and target/clax-bin/debug holds no kept binary, `ls` exits 1, `set -o pipefail` makes the pipeline fail, and `set -e` ends the script at this assignment, so the `test-bin: cargo build failed and no kept clax exists` message on line 15 is never printed. The exit code is still 1. Reproduced with `bash -c 'set -euo pipefail; newest=\"$(ls -t nothere/*/clax 2>/dev/null | awk \"NR == 1\")\"; echo reached'`, which exits 1 without printing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"b7582f533743fd6c577d000b1736a347a2418f6e37c74d990a79ab0a01289ce6"},"suggested_fix":"`newest=\"$(ls -t target/clax-bin/debug/*/clax 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR == 1' || true)\"`.","summary":"With no kept clax, test-bin.sh exits 1 silently: pipefail plus set -e end it at this assignment before its error message","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/test-bin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:07:37.346591Z","id":"c7fdf650550620c4a56f1ec5807d84bf1a42bbf8125ac9516134af35a2f05675","body":{"detail":"Copied to a scratch repository with a `cargo` shim that exits 101: with no kept clax it prints `test-bin: cargo build failed and no kept clax exists under target/clax-bin/debug` and exits 1; with one kept clax it prints the warning naming it and its absolute path, exit 0.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:33d400d1","summary":"The ls pipeline ends in `|| true`, so an empty store reaches the error message","supersedes":"6e05f24a5f6ccf69b2a41d92e1c3c94b8aab3d4527e7b8eaa18ecfc4349effbf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/pack_home.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:54:52.511791Z","id":"cb55a9b1708314506245a8988b8ff03c03d2c79424de9a212719b5efe333ed6c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: BundleReader.read (lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart) requires manifest.sig verified against author.key, and the installer, updater and trust rules key everything on the author key; a builtin source would need a new unsigned path through each of them, outside this change's files. The dedicated key keeps the shipped bundle an ordinary bundle the existing code installs and updates.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"025d88238e31d6786e356fd0cd6192bbb35f861ece165afbcac2790eedf1b0bb"},"summary":"An unsigned builtin home bundle, trusted because it ships inside the signed app package","tags":["signing","home-app","revisit:the installer gains a trust source for bundles read from the app's own assets","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/pack_home.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:00:08.530258Z","id":"61c2d4fa27ee1a6656744fdde1528c67cfcba74ae1d07316f47eae5714848804","body":{"detail":"keyFile.parent.createSync and writeAsStringSync use default permissions (0644/0755 under the usual umask 022). The header documents running it as dart run tool/pack_home.dart --key <file> --write.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"2d3c1160c6e1a4aab53bbe40bed4702e6c64d9289ad37160ca69f3158c979408"},"suggested_fix":"chmod 600 the file (Process.run('chmod', ['600', path]) on POSIX) after writing, or refuse to make a key unless invoked with a flag the script passes.","summary":"pack_home.dart writes the new signing seed with the process umask; run directly (not through scripts/build-home-bundle.sh, which sets umask 077) the seed file is world-readable","tags":["review","task:home-2","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/pack_home.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:15.751701Z","id":"2feb3f50cd64c56b302a132384c2f790281803f3ba887ba105a5da1d78052fdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:018d1a9d3","summary":"pack_home.dart no longer makes a seed: it reads the seed tool/home-version.sh names and stops when there is none ('no seed at <path>', pack_home.dart:127-128); `grep -n 'Random.secure\\|writeAsStringSync' apps/clax_app/tool/pack_home.dart` finds nothing","supersedes":"61c2d4fa27ee1a6656744fdde1528c67cfcba74ae1d07316f47eae5714848804","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/pack_home.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:15.956843Z","id":"caf4d23ecd91c4a21eff816f1187d3e370936b1aa7de4cebfbe47f1a2f67517f","body":{"detail":"Not taken: BundleReader.read (lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart) requires manifest.sig verified against author.key, and the installer, updater and trust rules key everything on the author key; a builtin source would need a new unsigned path through each of them. The dedicated key keeps the shipped bundle an ordinary bundle the existing code installs and updates.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"b7ae89a61929b500f479c34f013d2a183a2a746d2e9a682d7ce0e6b12cdc418d"},"summary":"An unsigned builtin home bundle, trusted because it ships inside the signed app package","supersedes":"cb55a9b1708314506245a8988b8ff03c03d2c79424de9a212719b5efe333ed6c","tags":["signing","home-app","revisit:the installer gains a trust source for bundles read from the app's own assets","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/home-version.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:16.530298Z","id":"355b0e36df5ccd1cbec6ae32aab546379fc2246d5757547e5d19ea07e596645d","body":{"detail":"Not taken: scripts/app-phone.sh builds a dirty tree from `git archive HEAD` (target/app-phone/tree), which has no .git, so stamping would need the count passed in; uncommitted edits keep HEAD's count while their content differs (the same version under two hashes reads as `conflict` in lib/bundle/trust.dart, not an update); a rebase or squash can lower the count, and two branches count differently. The ledger beside the release key (~/.config/clax/home-bundle/releases) gives every changed build on the releasing machine a higher version, committed or not, at the cost of machine-local state.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"729bdc4677b059725b4acdd5cd069fa0b3bc4752b9f75a6ee5aa24f1d7ce99ae"},"summary":"Home bundle version from git: the number of commits touching apps/clax_app/home and assets/kit, through Bazel's workspace status stamping","tags":["home-app","versioning","revisit:the home app is released from more than one machine, or from CI with the release key","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/home-version.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:16.530371Z","id":"b96e8b27640054897352d68855af190fe8059a0142032797a9955c3185ce3289","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it keeps a step per home change (raise version, rebuild), which is what the automatic ledger removes, and a forgotten bump fails the build only after the change is made. Its merit: versions live in the repository, so a lost ledger or a second releasing machine cannot reorder them. home/manifest.json's `version` remains as the floor built versions start above, so raising it by hand still works.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"729bdc4677b059725b4acdd5cd069fa0b3bc4752b9f75a6ee5aa24f1d7ce99ae"},"summary":"Hand-bumped home bundle version in home/manifest.json, with a check that fails when the sources change without a bump","tags":["home-app","versioning","revisit:the ledger is lost or out of step with what installs have","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/home-version.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:16.530408Z","id":"8a42e334efd83c2d39fcff17b61c613a51ce65e567e7c69985243e6e8f0d2cc1","body":{"detail":"So CI and machines without ~/.config/clax/home-bundle/key still build //apps/clax_app:apk and run its tests. A dev-signed bundle is on another lineage under another key than the release, so lib/bundle/trust.dart decide() answers `foreign`/`install` for it on an install of the released home app, never `update`, and home_bundle_test refuses a non-release key on the release lineage. Accepted risk: on a device whose home app came from such a build, anyone holding the public seed can sign an update to that home app (which holds the home capability). Only builds from machines without the key are affected; bazel/flutter/home_release.bzl prints a DEBUG line naming the missing key when it falls back.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"69f0dc87ef71a6009ecbf6a44378ecba0603684fb5dca410f922b22deb04b71c"},"summary":"Without the release key the home bundle is signed by apps/clax_app/tool/home-dev.key, a committed seed anyone can read, on home/manifest.json's dev_lineage","tags":["signing","home-app","revisit:Clax ships APKs or macOS apps built on CI to people","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/ios-app-check.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:15:15.148306Z","id":"55137e5973fa444b7c4c297be8084489e4bc09ffb7b25886a58f4574327b021f","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter's flutter_ios_privacy_manifests (flutter/private/flutter_ios_application.bzl:357-390) symlinks each plugin's PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy to '__ios_app_privacy_manifests___<path>_PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy' and passes them as ios_application resources, so nine files with that suffix land at the root of Clax.app (file_picker, flutter_local_notifications, flutter_secure_storage, flutter_timezone, geolocator, image_picker, package_info_plus, share_plus, webview_flutter_wkwebview). Its doc says Apple's submission validator finds them all; nothing here has shown that. This check only proves they are in the bundle and parse. The first TestFlight upload's privacy report (or Xcode's Generate Privacy Report on the archive) settles it; if they are not read, the app's own ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy must carry the plugins' required-reason entries.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"6c9b24fa844d42a713c75db4a17a7aa87cb942fc1a3c8f5802a5c15aecdd524b"},"summary":"The plugins' privacy manifests sit at Clax.app's root under flattened names, not as PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy in a bundle of their own; whether App Store Connect reads them is unverified","tags":["revisit:first TestFlight upload's privacy report","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/macos-app-check.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:17:18.003932Z","id":"5a8c3278a2ac1d295227c9fbfa5d4a696b3321d9f97ebaa57748a1dbd759f8c7","body":{"detail":"The Mac app carries the core as Contents/Frameworks/libclax_embed.dylib and no clax helper; crates/clax-embed/src binds no socket (git grep -n 'TcpListener\\|bind(' -- crates/clax-embed/src finds nothing). Release.entitlements:15 and DebugProfile.entitlements:15 still grant com.apple.security.network.server, and macos-app-check.sh:254 requires it. Keeping it is harmless to the app but widens the sandbox for nothing; dropping it means editing both entitlements files and this check. Owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":257},"content_hash":"367de74b150fe44cfeaf6d7e7151cba673faef18387618bd64210caa19268073"},"summary":"The Mac app still asks for com.apple.security.network.server, which the embedded core does not need: should it go?","tags":["status:needs-decision","core","macos","entitlements","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/test-bin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.703983Z","id":"0f996eff81bd660befcabbec933f118dcdac6eb6a9ee25555b462e42748e1d94","body":{"detail":"The *_real_test.dart files open the embedded core (test/support/real_core.dart, CLAX_EMBED_LIB); apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel no longer gives the real suite //crates/clax-cli:clax. scripts/run.sh:292 and scripts/quality_gates.sh:163 still build a clax and pass CLAX_TEST_BIN to tool/check.sh, and a native `flutter test` run gets no CLAX_EMBED_LIB, so its real tests skip.","kind":"concern","summary":"No app test reads CLAX_TEST_BIN any more: tool/test-bin.sh is used only by scripts/run.sh's native app check","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
